  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia Tech Applied Research has $314M in contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. Georgia Tech Applied Research received 148 awards this period, with an average award size of $2.1M, and obligations fell 34.0% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $314M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market with $272M in obligations. Engineering Services accounts for $35.5M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $7.5M. Georgia Tech Applied Research also shows obligations in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $1M and Research and Development in Nanotechnology at $422K. Fiscal-year history shows prior totals of $581M in FY21, $652M in FY22, $675M in FY23, $513M in FY24, and $475M in FY25, illustrating the multi-year scale of contracting activity. Current-year totals are partial, and award-value figures in some tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
