        "heading": "Who are the main buyers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $314M to Georgia Tech Applied Research in FY2026 to date. Other named agencies show much smaller recorded obligations in the available tables. The buying profile is concentrated, with the Department of Defense accounting for the vast majority of recorded obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the primary products and markets for these contracts?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounts for $272M in obligations. Engineering Services accounts for $35.5M, and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounts for $7.5M. Georgia Tech Applied Research also records obligations in Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $1M and Research and Development in Nanotechnology at $422K."
      }
    ]
